# Postgres connection (Supabase pooler URL or local). Required by the dashboard
# and by the scripts in scripts/.
TCA_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:pass@host:6543/postgres

# QuickNode archive endpoint for Base mainnet. debug_traceTransaction + eth_call
# at historical block heights require an archive plan, AND the trace methods
# require QuickNode's paid Trace Mode add-on — it is off by default, and without
# it the decoder produces no receipts at all rather than degrading. Required.
#
# QuickNode also caps eth_getLogs at a 10,000-block RANGE (HTTP 413 past it, no
# matter how few logs match); refreshReactors.ts CHUNK_BLOCKS is sized to that.
#
# Note: the RPC e2e tests skip silently unless this is EXPORTED, and `source .env`
# does not export. Use: set -a && source .env && set +a
TCA_RPC_URL=https://YOUR-ENDPOINT.base-mainnet.quiknode.pro/YOUR_TOKEN/

# ── Access gate (REQUIRED — the app serves nothing without both) ─────────────
# A shared-password gate over every page AND every API route, standing in until
# a real auth suite lands. It deliberately fails CLOSED: if either value is
# missing, all requests get 503 rather than silently running wide open, because
# a missing env var in production is exactly how an app ends up public.
#
# APP_ACCESS_PASSWORD is what users type on /login.
# APP_SESSION_SECRET signs the session cookie — rotate it to log everyone out.
# Generate one with: openssl rand -base64 32
APP_ACCESS_PASSWORD=
APP_SESSION_SECRET=

# Optional rate limits, per client IP per minute. Defaults shown.
# A fresh receipt analysis is ~40 RPC calls, so ANALYSES is the one that guards
# the bill; REQUESTS is a cheaper ceiling on cache hits; DIAGNOSIS covers the
# GET /?tx= path, which spends RPC on a cache miss and needs no JS to trigger.
# NOTE: these counters live in process memory, which is correct for a single
# container (Railway) but NOT for a multi-instance/serverless deploy — there,
# each instance keeps its own counters and the effective limit multiplies by the
# instance count. Swap the store in lib/rateLimit.ts for Redis before scaling out.
# RATE_LIMIT_ANALYSES_PER_MIN=20
# RATE_LIMIT_REQUESTS_PER_MIN=120
# RATE_LIMIT_DIAGNOSIS_PER_MIN=30

# Optional. Free Etherscan V2 key, used to name verified fee-sink contracts on
# the receipt (getsourcecode). Without it those lines fall back to a generic
# "[Aggregator] Fee" label — nothing else degrades.
ETHERSCAN_API_KEY=

# Optional, currently inert. The Dune ETH/USD oracle is wired up but disabled:
# DUNE_ETH_USD_QUERY_ID in packages/core/src/duneOracle.ts is still 0. Setting
# this key alone does nothing.
# DUNE_API_KEY=
